{#
  build/review.j2 — review prompt for the build workflow.

  Evaluates the implementation against the originating Linear ticket.
  Reviewer also authors the commit message from what was actually built.

  Required state: ticket_title, ticket_description (written by fetch-ticket).
  Required inputs: linear_id.
  submit_tool_name injected by the contract engine.
#}
Review the implementation of Linear ticket {{ inputs.linear_id }} — **{{ state.ticket_title }}**.

## Acceptance criteria

{{ state.ticket_description }}

## Review criteria

Evaluate against: correctness relative to the acceptance criteria above, adequate test coverage, focused diff (no drive-by changes), no obvious regressions. Read the diff or relevant files, then identify issues. Tag each finding with HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW.

Be concrete — point to file and line where possible. A clean review (no findings) is a valid result; do not invent issues to fill space.

## Commit message

Once you have read the diff, write a commit message describing what was actually built — not the ticket title. Format: `type(scope): description` where type is one of `feat / fix / chore / refactor / test`. One line, under 72 characters.

When done, call {{ submit_tool_name | default('submit') }} exactly once with the verdict, issues list, and commit message.
